// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/t27os/godmode_001.t27 -- GODMODE-001 end to end: one task through contract, policy, supervisor, journal,
; bounded retry, the five completion gates and the final report, as one pure decision walk.
; The host does the effects (git worktree, PTY spawn, the command, git status, the artifact check, the clock) and hands
; the walk what it observed; the walk returns every decision the host must journal and report. Nothing here runs a
; process, so the same walk is the oracle for any executor (the reference local shell executor today, another later).
; One observation for the first attempt and one for every retry: a host that saw a fresh result per retry feeds them
; one walk at a time; the walk with `again == first` is the "the same failure every time" case the brief names.
; The approval path: v1 has no approver. A task whose only contract failure is a dangerous command (GM-E027 with a
; CV_DANGEROUS verdict) journals task.validated (code 27: the contract was read and checked), approval.requested,
; approval.denied and task.failed, and ends `denied`. Any other contract failure journals task.failed alone and ends
; `rejected`. Neither path starts a worktree, a PTY or a command.
; A run that never reached the gates reports every gate as not passed (G_ALL): nothing was verified, so nothing passed.
; Pure module, no @extern. Acceptance tests A-E of the GODMODE v1 brief map to the tests below by their names.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

